		'long'     => <<<'HTML'
<h2>Refrigeration that drives convenience sales</h2>
<p>In a convenience store, chilled and frozen ranges bring customers in several times a week: milk, sandwiches, meal deals, cold drinks and ice cream. The refrigeration has to hold a lot of stock in a small floor area, keep it safe through long opening hours and make it easy to pick up. This page covers the cabinets convenience stores, newsagents, farm shops and campus stores use most; for fuel station shops, see <a href="/markets/forecourts/">forecourt display fridges</a>.</p>

<h2>The core of a convenience store</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Multideck fridges</strong> – open self-service fridges for dairy, cooked meats, sandwiches and ready meals, from 600 mm to 1800 mm wide. The slimline models are only 600 mm deep, so aisles stay clear.</li>
<li><strong>Shutter multidecks</strong> – lockable shutters secure stock overnight, ideal for late-night stores and shared sites.</li>
<li><strong>Glass door drinks chillers</strong> – single, double and sliding door models (about 307 to 806 litres) for soft drinks, water, beer and energy drinks, with far lower running costs than open fridges.</li>
<li><strong>Display freezers</strong> – upright glass door freezers for ready meals and ice cream tubs, and a sliding glass lid chest freezer for lollies and impulse lines.</li>
<li><strong>Hot food displays</strong> – a hot multideck or a dual temperature multideck for pasties, sausage rolls and breakfast rolls next to the chilled meal deal.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Planning chilled space</h2>
<p>Plan in linear metres. Give dairy and milk a destination position at the back of the store, so customers walk past other ranges; put food-to-go and cold drinks near the entrance and the till; and keep frozen near the end of the shopping trip. Widths can be combined to fill a wall exactly – for example a 1500 mm and a 1200 mm multideck give 2.7 metres of chilled display.</p>

<h2>Running costs over long opening hours</h2>
<ul>
<li>Use the night blind or shutter on every open fridge as soon as the store closes.</li>
<li>Sell bottled drinks from glass door chillers rather than open shelves.</li>
<li>Keep cabinets away from entrance doors, heaters and sunny windows – open fridges are designed for rooms up to about 25 °C.</li>
<li>Clean condensers regularly and replace split door gaskets.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Delivery and installation</h2>
<p>Multidecks are heavy – about 247 kg for a 1200 mm slimline model and up to 410 kg for an 1800 mm shutter multideck – so check doors, steps and the floor before delivery. If a store is open while equipment is replaced, add Removal &amp; Disposal of the old unit to take it away on the same visit.</p>
